<title>UK: ICO coffee exports up slightly in November.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports up slightly in November.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Coffee Organization (ICO) exporting members' exports rose slightly to 6.08 million 60-kg bags in November from 6.03 million in October and 6.02 million in November 1995, ICO figures showed.</p>
<p>In the year from December 1995 to November 1996, total exports were 73.81 million bags, up from 66.19 million in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included:</p>
<p>			 Nov 96    Nov 95     Dec95/Nov96  Dec94/Nov95</p>
<p>    Total	    6,077     6,019	73,816	 66,194</p>
<p>    Brazil	   1,808     1,004	14,332	 14,938</p>
<p>    Colombia	 1,236     1,100	10,880	  9,495</p>
<p>    Uganda	     436	 289	 4,518	  2,928</p>
<p>    Indonesia	  365	 555	 5,634	  3,744</p>
<p>    Vietnam	    236	 445	 3,419	  3,540</p>
<p>    Mexico	     214	 296	 4,561	  3,464</p>
<p>    Guatemala	  209	 252	 3,663	  3,699</p>
<p>    Ecuador	    138	 123	 1,441	  1,459</p>
<p>    El Salvador	136	 176	 2,294	  1,846</p>
<p>    Costa Rica	 134	 194	 2,405	  2,018</p>
<p>    India		 90	 296	 2,825	  2,355</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast	 76	 144	 2,612	  2,435</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
